<title>SWITZERLAND: Zurich declines comment on Scudder talk.</title>
<headline>Zurich declines comment on Scudder talk.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A spokeswoman at Zurich Insurance Group said the company could not comment on a New York Times report that it was near a deal to buy  Scudder, Stevens &amp; Clark, the U.S. money management firm.</p>
<p>&quot;I am very sorry, but due to company policy, we can't comment on rumours,&quot; said Iris Roth, group spokeswoman for Zurich in response to an enquiry.</p>
<p>She was responding to a query following a report in Friday's edition of the New York Times that the Swiss insurer was considering such a deal, which the newspaper said was worth $1.5 billion.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
